# Data: the HAND source files, gauge and NWM forcing, and the prewarmed reference run are
# tracked so teammates can run the engine after `flood prep hand` rebuilds the cube locally.
# The cube itself (1.2 GB of dense arrays) and superseded runs stay out of git.
data/*
!data/hand/
!data/usgs/
!data/nwm/
data/**/*.part
data/nwm/**/raw/
runs/*
!runs/kerr-2025-07-04-replay-fe0f78/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
tests/fixtures/mini_huc/out/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Manually acquired source PDFs, verified source manifests, and generated local AAR indices.
# (covered by data/* above, called out here for clarity)

# The demographic risk model's data. Its own rule on purpose: the `data/*`
# above is anchored to the repo root and does NOT match project/data, unlike
# the bare `data/` it replaced.
#
# The raw pulls (240 MB) stay out -- four of their six sources are pinned in
# the URL, so re-fetching is deterministic. The three derived tables are
# committed gzipped because the OpenFEMA query is not date-pinned and they are
# the only reproducibility record for the scores in
# project/logs/final_summary.log. Loaders prefer a local .csv and fall back.
project/data/*
!project/data/processed/
project/data/processed/*
!project/data/processed/*.csv.gz
